  "notes": [
    {
      "reusableRuntime": "PrimeRuntime.generate(messages:options:) and PrimeRuntimeLoader in prime-runtime; backend adapters MLXPrimeRuntime and CoreMLPrimeRuntime load declared model bundles and use their compatible tokenizers.",
      "neuralKitRole": "PrimeRuntimeSession owns a loaded runtime; PrimeAskBrain wraps session loading and proposal. NeuralKit is already a separate Swift package rather than the PMHNP app target.",
      "remainingDomainCoupling": "Both backend generate methods invoke PrimeStudyPrompt.normalizeForGeneration. It allows exactly one user message and routes screening severity prompts through PrimeSeatKit to append Clinical meaning:. PrimeStudyWire also applies study framing. These are PMHNP-specific conventions within otherwise reusable loading/generation code.",
      "nativeEngineReuse": "NativeTinyDecoder.forward(tokenIds:positionOffset:) is shared by explicitly separate PMHNP, Latin and compositional profiles. NativeLabCheckpoint.loadWeights loads the selected checkpoint. PMHNP is one corpus/tokenizer/profile, not the definition of the neural engine.",
      "appSpecificVerification": "PrimeChatModelEndpoint.disposeModelDraft may substitute reference text after generation and marks that channel modelHybridGold; reply also has a fixed social-response branch. Use raw model helpers for the cross-domain comparison, retaining model output separately from deterministic answers.",
      "practicalNextBoundary": "Keep model loading, tokenization and raw generation reusable. Make study framing and PMHNP verification explicit app adapters. Attach corpus/export registries to model experiments without changing existing tokenizers or claiming the source catalog has trained the model."
    }
  ]
